{"id": "RT-science-genetics", "body": {"t": "main", "a": {"class": "wrap", "id": "main-content"}, "c": [" ", " ", {"t": "p", "a": {"class": "kicker"}, "c": ["Confirmed science / Genetics"]}, " ", {"t": "h1", "c": ["Genetics and ADHD: start here"]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "article-meta"}, "c": [{"t": "span", "a": {"class": "badge"}, "c": ["Last updated 30 September 2026"]}, {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "badge"}, "c": ["GEN-00"]}]}, " ", {"t": "details", "a": {"class": "toc", "open": "true"}, "c": [{"t": "summary", "c": ["On this page"]}, {"t": "ol", "c": [{"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#choose-a-genetics-topic"}, "c": ["Choose a genetics topic"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#what-needs-distinguishing"}, "c": ["What needs distinguishing"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#reading-order"}, "c": ["Reading order"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#how-every-article-in-the-series-is-built"}, "c": ["How every article in the series is built"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#evidence-tiers-used-in-this-series"}, "c": ["Evidence tiers used in this series"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#what-this-evidence-can-tell-us"}, "c": ["What this evidence can tell us"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#sources"}, "c": ["Sources"]}]}]}]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "article-body gen-article"}, "c": [" ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "choose-a-genetics-topic"}, "c": ["Choose a genetics topic"]}, " ", {"t": "ul", "c": [{"t": "li", "c": ["ADHD runs in families. Twin studies put ", {"t": "a", "a": {"class": "gloss", "href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/#g-heritability", "title": "The proportion of differences in a trait across a population that is explained by genetic differences. It is not the proportion of any one person's condition"}, "c": ["heritability"]}, " at about 74% (", {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "tier tier-b"}, "c": ["Tier B"]}, ")."]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["There is no single \"ADHD gene\". The picture is thousands of common variants that each nudge risk a tiny amount, plus rarer variants with bigger effects, plus chance and environment (", {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "tier tier-b"}, "c": ["Tier B"]}, ")."]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["Genes describe ", {"t": "strong", "c": ["risk"]}, ". They are not a diagnostic test and they do not tell a clinician which medication to use (", {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "tier tier-b"}, "c": ["Tier B"]}, ")."]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["Some rare single-gene conditions affect the same dopamine pathways and can produce movement symptoms. That is a ", {"t": "strong", "c": ["differential diagnosis"]}, " question for specialists, not proof that ADHD is caused by those genes (", {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "tier tier-a"}, "c": ["Tier A"]}, " for the conditions, ", {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "tier tier-d"}, "c": ["Tier D"]}, " for any link to ADHD)."]}]}, " ", {"t": "figure", "a": {"class": "fig", "id": "fig-two-counts"}, "c": [" ", {"t": "img", "a": {"src": "/assets/figures/genetics-two-registers.svg", "width": "720", "height": "420", "loading": "lazy", "alt": "Schematic: two separate boxes, a 2023 study with 27 loci and a 2025 study with 39 loci, not added together."}}, " ", {"t": "figcaption", "c": [{"t": "span", "a": {"class": "fig-label"}, "c": ["Schematic, not a data chart"]}, " ", {"t": "strong", "c": ["Two studies, two counts."]}, " Demontis and colleagues (2023) reported 27 genome-wide significant regions from ADHD diagnosis data (", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41588-022-01285-8", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["DOI"]}, "). van der Laan and colleagues (2025) combined childhood symptom scores with diagnosis data and reported 39, of which 17 were new (", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41588-025-02295-y", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["DOI"]}, "). The designs differ, so the counts are not a running total, and neither is a personal score. Details in ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-01/"}, "c": ["GEN-01"]}, " and ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-12/"}, "c": ["GEN-12"]}, "."]}, " "]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "what-needs-distinguishing", "class": "sec sec-misread"}, "c": ["What needs distinguishing"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["\"It's genetic\" gets heard as \"one faulty gene\". The real finding is closer to \"many small dials and a few large switches\". Keeping those two pictures apart is the whole point of this series."]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "reading-order"}, "c": ["Reading order"]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "table-wrap", "role": "region", "aria-label": "Table"}, "c": [{"t": "table", "c": [{"t": "thead", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["#"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Article"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Read it when you want to know"]}]}]}, {"t": "tbody", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-01/"}, "c": ["GEN-01"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["ADHD and genes: what the evidence shows"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["The headline numbers and what they do and do not mean"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-02/"}, "c": ["GEN-02"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["How to read a genetic claim"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Whether a claim you have seen is strong, weak or oversold"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-03/"}, "c": ["GEN-03"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["The dopamine supply chain in plain English"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Which step does what, and which genes sit where"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-04/"}, "c": ["GEN-04"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Common variants, rare variants and the heritability gap"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Why \"74%\" and \"about a third\" are both true"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-05/"}, "c": ["GEN-05"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Polygenic scores: what they can and cannot do"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Whether a DNA score can diagnose ADHD"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-06/"}, "c": ["GEN-06"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["When movement symptoms and ADHD traits overlap"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Which single-gene conditions clinicians consider"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["GEN-07 ", {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "hold"}, "c": ["in preparation"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Genes and medication"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["What ", {"t": "a", "a": {"class": "gloss", "href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/#g-pharmacogenomics", "title": "The study of how genes change the way the body handles a drug"}, "c": ["pharmacogenomics"]}, " does and does not cover"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["GEN-08 ", {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "hold"}, "c": ["in preparation"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Genetic testing on the NHS"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["What to ask for, what results can mean"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-09/"}, "c": ["GEN-09"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Family history and inheritance patterns"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["How to collect a family history that helps a clinician"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-10/"}, "c": ["GEN-10"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Autism genetics in brief"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Heritability, overlap with ADHD, and why it matters for care"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/"}, "c": ["GEN-11"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Glossary"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Any term you hit and do not recognise"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-12/"}, "c": ["GEN-12"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["The 27 ADHD risk ", {"t": "a", "a": {"class": "gloss", "href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/#g-locus", "title": "A region of DNA"}, "c": ["loci"]}, ": a closer look"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["A linked entry for each region in the 2023 study"]}]}]}]}]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "how-every-article-in-the-series-is-built"}, "c": ["How every article in the series is built"]}, " ", {"t": "ol", "c": [{"t": "li", "c": ["Short version"]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["The usual mix-up"]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["The plain-English layer"]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["The deeper layer (optional to read)"]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["Limits (what this does not claim)"]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["Sources"]}]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "evidence-tiers-used-in-this-series"}, "c": ["Evidence tiers used in this series"]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "table-wrap", "role": "region", "aria-label": "Table"}, "c": [{"t": "table", "c": [{"t": "thead", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Tier"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Meaning"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["How it is written"]}]}]}, {"t": "tbody", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["A"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Established biology, in textbooks and guidelines"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Stated plainly"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["B"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Robust ADHD evidence: large, replicated, or consensus reviews"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Stated plainly, source named"]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["C"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Preliminary, peripheral (e.g. blood cells), small or unreplicated"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["\"One small study found...\""]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["D"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Open hypothesis"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["\"One working idea is... It has not been tested in...\""]}]}]}]}]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "what-this-evidence-can-tell-us", "class": "sec sec-limit"}, "c": ["What this evidence can tell us"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["This series explains the science. It does not diagnose, and it does not replace a clinician or a genetics service. Population findings describe groups; they do not predict one person."]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "sources", "class": "sec sec-src"}, "c": ["Sources"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["See each article. Bibliographic details for papers cited in this series were checked against PubMed."]}, " "]}, " ", {"t": "p", "a": {"class": "gloss-hint"}, "c": ["Underlined terms link to the ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/"}, "c": ["glossary"]}, "; hover or long-press for a quick definition."]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "nextbox"}, "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Useful next destination."]}, " Start with ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-01/"}, "c": ["GEN-01"]}, ", then ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-02/"}, "c": ["GEN-02"]}, ". If you only read two, read those."]}, " ", {"t": "nav", "a": {"class": "gen-series", "aria-label": "Genetics series"}, "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/"}, "c": ["All genetics articles"]}, {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/"}, "c": ["Glossary"]}, {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/sources/numbers/"}, "c": ["Verified numbers"]}]}, " "]}}